# Responsive redesign — active task context

## Scope constraint (CRITICAL)

Desktop (>1024px) layout is FINISHED and APPROVED.
Do not modify desktop styles unless explicitly requested.
All work happens inside `@media (max-width: 1024px)` and `@media (max-width: 768px)` blocks.

Before modifying any CSS rule, check whether it's inside a media query.
If it's a base/desktop rule, do not touch it — override it inside a responsive block instead.

## Breakpoints (from DESIGN.md)

- Desktop: > 1024px — locked, do not change
- Tablet: 768px – 1024px — needs rebuild
- Mobile: < 768px — needs rebuild

Test viewports:
- 1440×900 (desktop baseline — must not regress)
- 1024×768 (tablet landscape — iPad)
- 820×1180 (tablet portrait — iPad Air)
- 414×896 (large phone — iPhone 11 Pro Max)
- 390×844 (mid phone — iPhone 12/13/14)
- 360×800 (small phone — common Android)

## Known responsive problems (from the user)

- Landing page diagonal layout breaks on tablet
- Navigation unusable on mobile
- Project heroes / galleries layout issues on narrow viewports
- Mosaic column count needs verification across sizes

## Source-of-truth docs

- `CLAUDE.md` — workflow guardrails
- `DESIGN.md` — design system + breakpoint table
- `EXTENSION_PLAN.md` — feature history and schema v2

Read these before suggesting architectural changes.

## What not to do

- Do not refactor working desktop CSS "while you're in there"
- Do not introduce new CSS variables for responsive values unless a magic number repeats 3+ times
- Do not add JS-driven responsive behavior if CSS can handle it
- Do not use `display: none` to hide things on mobile without checking the element isn't needed for accessibility/context
- Do not change HTML structure; responsive should be CSS-only unless structure is genuinely broken